.Dd July 1, 2026
.Dt FANSD 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fansd
.Nd intelligent fan speed daemon for Dell servers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar file
.Op Fl debug
.Nm
.Fl init-config Ar file | Fl
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a daemon that continuously adjusts fan speed on Dell servers via IPMI.
It collects CPU temperature, drive temperature, and system load, maps each
reading to a fan speed percentage using linear interpolation across
configurable thresholds, and applies the highest resulting speed.
Speed increases take effect immediately; decreases are gated by a
hysteresis value to prevent rapid oscillation.
.Pp
CPU temperature is read from the
.Va dev.cpu.N.temperature
sysctls provided by the
.Xr coretemp 4
or
.Xr amdtemp 4
kernel module.
If those OIDs are absent,
.Nm
falls back to
.Xr sensors 1
.Pq lm-sensors
and then to
.Xr ipmitool 1
SDR readings.
.Pp
When
.Va prometheus.enabled
is set to true,
.Nm
also serves Prometheus text-format gauges at
.Pa /metrics
on the configured listen address
.Pq default Li :9105 .
.Pp
On receipt of
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Nm
restores BIOS automatic fan control before exiting.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl config Ar file
Path to the TOML configuration file.
Defaults to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/fansd/fansd.toml .
.It Fl debug
Enable debug-level structured logging.
Each poll cycle emits one line per sensor showing the raw reading and
the computed fan speed.
.It Fl init-config Ar file | Fl
Probe hardware and write a starter configuration to
.Ar file .
Pass
.Fl
to write to standard output.
.Nm
exits after writing the config; the daemon loop does not start.
.Pp
The following probes are performed:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Storage disks are enumerated via
.Xr sysctl 8
.Va kern.disks
.Pq Cm ada* , da* , nvd* , nda* .
Each candidate is queried with
.Xr smartctl 8
to exclude virtual or no-medium devices
.Pq e.g.\& iDRAC virtual floppy .
.It
Drive trip temperature is read from
.Xr smartctl 8
output
.Pq Qq Drive Trip Temperature
for SCSI/SAS, or from attribute 194 min/max for ATA.
Per-drive thresholds are derived as
.Cm max_temp No = trip\-5
and
.Cm min_temp No = max_temp\-15 .
Falls back to 35/55 when unavailable.
.It
CPU TjMax is read from
.Va dev.cpu.N.coretemp.tjmax
or
.Va dev.cpu.N.amdtemp.tjmax .
CPU thresholds are set to
.Cm max_temp No = TjMax\-5
and
.Cm min_temp No = max_temp\-30 .
Falls back to 50/80 when unavailable.
.It
System load thresholds are scaled by CPU count.
.El
.Pp
Drive probing requires root access to open raw disk devices.
When run without root,
.Nm
prints a warning to stderr and skips drive probing, including all detected
disks without filtering.
CPU TjMax probing does not require root.
.Pp
The generated IPMI credentials are placeholders and must be edited before use.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses TOML syntax.
.Ss [ipmi]
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va host
IP address or hostname of the Dell iDRAC.
.It Va user
IPMI username.
.It Va password
IPMI password.
.It Va interface
.Xr ipmitool 1
interface type.
Defaults to
.Cm lanplus .
.El
.Ss [fan]
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va min_speed
Minimum fan speed as a percentage (0\(en100).
Default: 10.
.It Va max_speed
Maximum fan speed as a percentage (0\(en100).
Default: 100.
.It Va poll_interval
Duration string
.Pq e.g. Cm 30s , 1m
controlling how often sensors are sampled.
Default:
.Cm 30s .
.It Va hysteresis
Fan speed must decrease by at least this many percentage points before
the lower speed is applied.
Increases are never gated.
Default: 5.
.El
.Ss [cpu]
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va enabled
Enable CPU temperature monitoring.
Default: true.
.It Va sensors_cmd
Path to the
.Xr sensors 1
binary used as the second-priority CPU temperature source.
Default:
.Cm sensors .
The priority order is:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Va dev.cpu.N.temperature
sysctls
.Pq Xr coretemp 4 No / Xr amdtemp 4
.It
.Xr sensors 1
.Pq lm-sensors
.It
.Xr ipmitool 1
SDR temperature readings
.El
.It Va min_temp
CPU temperature in \(deC at which
.Va fan.min_speed
applies.
Default: 50.
.It Va max_temp
CPU temperature in \(deC at which
.Va fan.max_speed
applies.
Default: 80.
.El
.Ss [load]
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va enabled
Enable system load monitoring.
Default: true.
.It Va min_load
Normalized load average
.Pq load / CPU count
at which
.Va fan.min_speed
applies.
Default: 1.0.
.It Va max_load
Normalized load average at which
.Va fan.max_speed
applies.
Default: 4.0.
.El
.Ss [[drives]]
One section per disk.
Multiple sections are supported.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va device
Block device path, e.g.\&
.Pa /dev/da0 .
.It Va min_temp
Drive temperature in \(deC at which
.Va fan.min_speed
applies.
.It Va max_temp
Drive temperature in \(deC at which
.Va fan.max_speed
applies.
.El
.Ss [prometheus]
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va enabled
Expose a Prometheus metrics endpoint.
Default: false.
.It Va listen
Address and port for the metrics HTTP server.
Default:
.Cm :9105 .
.El
.Pp
The following gauges are served at
.Pa /metrics
in Prometheus text exposition format:
.Bl -tag -width fansd_drive_temperature_celsius
.It Li fansd_cpu_temperature_celsius
Current CPU temperature in \(deC.
.It Li fansd_system_load_normalized
One-minute load average divided by CPU count.
.It Li fansd_fan_speed_percent
Current IPMI fan speed target as a percentage.
.It Li fansd_drive_temperature_celsius{device="..."}
Per-drive temperature in \(deC, one time series per configured device.
.El
.Pp
Metrics whose collector failed in the most recent poll cycle are omitted
from the output rather than reported as zero.
.Sh FAN SPEED CALCULATION
For each enabled sensor the current reading is linearly interpolated
between the configured lower and upper bounds:
.Pp
.D1 speed = min_speed + (value \- min_val) / (max_val \- min_val) * (max_speed \- min_speed)
.Pp
Readings at or below
.Va min_val
map to
.Va fan.min_speed ;
readings at or above
.Va max_val
map to
.Va fan.max_speed .
The daemon applies the highest speed returned by any sensor.
.Sh RC.D INTEGRATION
Install the bundled service script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
install -m 555 rc.d/fansd /usr/local/etc/rc.d/fansd
.Ed
.Pp
Enable the service in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fansd_enable="YES"
fansd_config="/usr/local/etc/fansd/fansd.toml"   # optional
fansd_flags="-debug"                              # optional
.Ed
.Pp
The rc.d script uses
.Xr daemon 8
with automatic restart
.Pq Fl r .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/fansd/fansd.toml
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /var/run/fansd.pid
PID file written by
.Xr daemon 8 .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/fansd
rc.d service script.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a starter config (root required for accurate drive detection):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo fansd -init-config /usr/local/etc/fansd/fansd.toml
.Ed
.Pp
Preview the generated config on stdout without writing a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo fansd -init-config -
.Ed
.Pp
Run in the foreground with debug logging:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fansd -config /usr/local/etc/fansd/fansd.toml -debug
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipmitool 1 ,
.Xr sensors 1 ,
.Xr smartctl 8 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
